        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What is \"The 1975\"?\n\nAnswer A: The 1975\n  about: The 1975\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"The 1975 were selling out shows even before the debut of their full length as Healy recalls in an interview with \"The AU Review\".\"\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: a band\n  about: The 1975\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"and they 've been making music together since age 13 . Prior to becoming the band 's lead singer and rhythm guitarist with the occasional piano , Healy originally played drums .\" [document 2]\n\nAnswer C: a protest song and a work of ambient music\n  about: The 1975\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"The 1975 \" is a protest song and a work of ambient music, where Thunberg delivers a spoken word performance.\" [document 3]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Mike Crossey, known for his work with Arctic Monkeys and Foals. The 1975 were selling out shows even before the debut of their full length as Healy recalls in an interview with \"The AU Review\". The lead single is a re-worked \"Sex\", which was released on 26 August 2013. The song premiered on Zane Lowe's BBC Radio 1 show on 8 July 2013, and a music video premiered on YouTube on 26 July. \"The 1975\" debuted at number one on the UK Albums Chart. The 1975 toured in the UK in September 2013, among others performing in Kingston upon Hull\nDocument 2: and they 've been making music together since age 13 . Prior to becoming the band 's lead singer and rhythm guitarist with the occasional piano , Healy originally played drums . The musician told GQ about The 1975 's beginnings , explaining that he was approached by Adam Hann 's girlfriend at the time , who was recruiting on Hann 's behalf : `` 'My boyfriend wants to start a band and knows that you play drums , ' '' Healy recalled her saying . `` We all met up , and I was the drummer , and I\nDocument 3: On Notes on a Conditional Form , the opening song deviates from the standard set of lyrics . [ 11 ] Lasting 4 minutes and 57 seconds , `` The 1975 '' is a protest song and a work of ambient music , where Thunberg delivers a spoken word performance . [ 9 ] [ 14 ] [ 15 ] [ 16 ] The lyrics call for civil disobedience to bring about reduction of greenhouse gas emissions in response to climate change , based on the January 2019 speech `` Our House Is on Fire `` , which Thunberg delivered\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
